{"canonical_record":{"canonical_payload_sha256":"5d0abe0244320ded1896b331a0c0d9b5d91cc857aeaab2cfeba9a1166d460d29","full_review_record_id":"fullrev_f6e69892edc8649ef95d9881d526ebae669e57a28fbe358748e3bb6c5cd292d3","overall_assessment":"The paper presents a technical contribution to online transfer learning for sequential data. The supplied evidence is insufficient to determine compliance with specific venue policies regarding anonymity, plagiarism, or broader impact documentation. The paper contains visible author names and affiliations, and uses clinical and personal data without explicit statements on consent, ethics approval, or data licensing.","paper_id":"ByqiJIqxg","paper_identity_sha256":"314dfb05ec1004247d6e8ac0efd70bbfbfc3d0948f46181cc5ce807ad90f5aa7","prompt_identity_sha256":"2ed86019d9fe9d2f9e45e3b88f24651512fa1888a90dac324b27ac289f8d7126","raw_response_sha256":"7fa048cef926a53539d9ea04002fa25e56c2093653f58f6adf4e1b6d739e8451","request_identity_sha256":"c60554d50bbae4a3b0940eb043e00f29c2fb0b545eb533e5dd23806f478cbd65","reviewer_identity_sha256":"c1cd7c7fdd4a2cbeb45c2f21af982ad0f30bffae8ae148e3eba36479685cf360","role":"POL","schema_version":"agentreview-full-review-corpus-v4","structural_context_sha256":"61588d8f9a9911eaefac772278ee145442f8e5ed3853da8363f2cfc003a74c03","subdimension_sections":[{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-038","SRC-039"],"review_text":"The paper applies the proposed method to sleep stage classification using clinical data from patients with Parkinson's disease and healthy subjects. While the paper notes that sleep disruption leads to health issues and that the method could improve quality of life, it does not discuss potential ethical risks, such as the accuracy of automated diagnosis in clinical settings, the potential for misdiagnosis, or the impact on patient care. There is no discussion of fairness or bias in the model's performance across different patient populations (e.g., healthy vs. Parkinson's patients) beyond the general motivation for the study.","subdimension_id":"POL-ETH"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-034","SRC-040"],"review_text":"The paper uses data from 19 participants for activity recognition and 142 patients for sleep classification. For the sleep data, the paper states that recordings were obtained from a clinical neurophysiology laboratory in Toronto (name anonymized) and manually scored. However, the paper does not explicitly state that informed consent was obtained from the participants or patients, nor does it mention any ethics committee approval (IRB) for the use of this data in the study. For the activity recognition data, it is described as part of an 'on-going study to promote physical activity,' but again, no specific details on consent or privacy protections are provided.","subdimension_id":"POL-DAT"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-001"],"review_text":"The paper lists the full names of the authors (Priyank Jain, Zhitang Chen, etc.) and their institutional affiliations (University of Waterloo, Huawei Technologies, Veedata Inc.) on the first page. It also provides email addresses for the authors. Without a frozen venue policy confirming whether double-blind review was required for this specific submission, it is not possible to declare a policy violation. However, the presence of these identifiers is a factual observation relevant to anonymity considerations.","subdimension_id":"POL-ANO"},{"paper_anchor_ids":[],"review_text":"The supplied evidence does not contain information regarding plagiarism, self-plagiarism, or dual submission. The paper cites relevant prior work, including the authors' own previous publications (Jaini & Poupart, 2016; Jaini et al., 2016), which is standard academic practice. There is no evidence in the text to suggest uncredited reuse of material or simultaneous submission to other venues.","subdimension_id":"POL-PLG"},{"paper_anchor_ids":[],"review_text":"The paper does not include a broader impact statement, a checklist for responsible AI, or explicit documentation of software/data licenses. While the paper mentions the use of a 'publicly available dataset' for the flow direction prediction task, it does not specify the license terms for this data or the code used in the experiments. The absence of these elements is noted, but without a frozen policy obligation, it is not possible to determine if their omission constitutes a compliance issue.","subdimension_id":"POL-IMP"}]},"disposition":"CANONICAL_FULL_REVIEW_COMMITTED","item_commit_sha256":"d3d4c334dfd4f18db7fdabe3cad1f3e92adc717871d32e7b893a7b7e1cc3c012","paper_id":"ByqiJIqxg","paper_ordinal":80,"raw_attempts":[{"assistant_content_base64":"","assistant_content_sha256":"7fa048cef926a53539d9ea04002fa25e56c2093653f58f6adf4e1b6d739e8451","attempt_index":0,"error":"","finish_reason":"stop","paper_id":"ByqiJIqxg","raw_provider_response_base64":"","raw_provider_response_sha256":"70f4f6f3b5050db9bb00f50bfd19d3b2bdcd7313247d57ecc502b4f2ecb6c939","request_identity_sha256":"c60554d50bbae4a3b0940eb043e00f29c2fb0b545eb533e5dd23806f478cbd65","role":"POL","schema_version":"no-memory-full-review-corpus-build-v5","usage":{"completion_tokens":846,"prompt_tokens":19090,"prompt_tokens_details":null,"total_tokens":19936},"valid":true}],"request_identity_sha256":"c60554d50bbae4a3b0940eb043e00f29c2fb0b545eb533e5dd23806f478cbd65","role":"POL","role_ordinal":4,"schema_version":"corpus-build-bootstrap-checkpoint-v4"}